{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchPlain::{{getvar::ariaPatchPlain}}- Method: fix what this speaker wants from the exchange and how they currently feel, read from their card, mood and what just happened, then voice exactly that as THIS character would, with their vocabulary, their rhythm, the things they avoid saying and the things they say too often. Each line pursues what the speaker wants in the moment. Reactions are sized to what actually caused them, as that character would weigh it.
}}{{addvar::ariaPatchPlainLines::1}}{{else}}{{trim}}
Method: fix what this speaker wants from the exchange and how they currently feel, read from their card, mood and what just happened, then voice exactly that as THIS character would, with their vocabulary, their rhythm, the things they avoid saying and the things they say too often. Each line pursues what the speaker wants in the moment. Reactions are sized to what actually caused them, as that character would weigh it.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "KIMIQWEN"}}{{// For Kimi and Qwen. It turns one-word orders into full sentences and keeps native thinking to one quick pass through The Logic Core's lines. Its filler-word rule sits at the end of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, the spot where Realistic Frankenstein put its GLM fix: it cuts the filler word these models put in characters' mouths before every decision, while nervous characters keep their stammers. GLM has a patch of its own. Use one model patch at most. }}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Filler: steadying or self-talk filler becomes the specific thought it held or the action; answering someone, it stands once.}}{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchPlain::{{getvar::ariaPatchPlain}}- One-word sentences for calls to action break the flow and immersion of the text. You need to make them at least two words long.
}}{{addvar::ariaPatchPlainLines::1}}{{trim}}
Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.{{else}}{{trim}}
One-word sentences for calls to action break the flow and immersion of the text. You need to make them at least two words long.
Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "DEEPSEEK"}}{{// For DeepSeek V4, Pro and Flash. It keeps native thinking to one short pass through The Logic Core's lines with no rule audits, since DeepSeek otherwise thinks for a minute or two before every reply and writes worse the longer it thinks. u/BSPiotr caught it saying your words back to you and replaying the same fact or beat for several turns, and V4 Pro gave a character a tail her card never mentioned, so three lines go to the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate and into the plan: answer your words without repeating them, let a fact or beat return only when the story changes it, and add no tail or other non-human part to a character whose card describes a body without one. V4 Pro (0813) also writes in fragments, so a fourth line, Joins, joins every short sentence after a reply's first one to its neighbour and folds a one-sentence paragraph into the one before it when the same speaker or the narration carries on, while stammers, cut-off lines and one-word answers stay. With 🔦 Flash Gate ON, as Flash users run it, Joins and the Flash Gate's Runs line both stay out, so Flash's prose should stay as it was. With 🥰 Bonds Lite or 🎲 Fate & Chekhov Ledger ON, the plan also gets a Tally line. In testing, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash left Sparks, Grudge and BOND at their starting numbers turn after turn, so Tally has it write each pair's old numbers, name this turn's warm acts, slights and sincere repairs, halve gains while Grudge is 3 or more, clear Grudge on a repair, turn 7 Sparks into BOND +1 and 5 Grudge into BOND -1, and write the new numbers, then update the 🎲 ledger's q and hp counters and its last entry. The Tally line sits outside the thinking word cap, stays in the plan and out of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, and is absent while both modules are off. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash users switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too. On a quantised route such as NanoGPT's, pick the 🧪 Auto-Routing Quality Hardener as well: the gate's Count line then names and-chains, and its Ledger line calls a reply that stops at the prose unfinished, so the 🎲 and 💚 blocks stop going missing. Use one model patch at most. }}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Echo: a character confirms or answers {{user}}'s line through an act or their own words, never by repeating it, single words included.
- Repeats: a fact, number or description once told is retold only when the story changes it; a played beat moves on.
- Bodies: when the card or first message describes a body, a part a plain human lacks, tails and wings included, appears only if named there, whatever the species or kind; an unnamed one goes unmentioned, hidden or absent alike.}}{{#if core_modules not contains "FLASH"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchJoins::- Joins: past one a reply, a spoken or narrated sentence under five words joins the sentence beside it with a comma or conjunction, a nervous card's stalls, cut-off lines and one-word answers aside; a one-sentence paragraph after the first joins the paragraph before it when the same speaker or the narration carries on.}}{{/if}}{{#if world_engine contains "BONDS"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: per pair, last BOND/Sparks/Grudge (strangers 0/0/0); this turn's listed act, slight and sincere repair, each or none; Sparks +1 per act (max +2, halved while Grudge >= 3), Grudge +1 per slight, repair sets Grudge 0; Sparks >= 7: BOND +1, Sparks 0; Grudge >= 5: BOND -1, Grudge 0; then the new three.{{#if world_engine contains "FATE"}} 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT, else 0; hp counts [hot] Bullets after this turn's loads, prunes and firings; last is this turn's tier, source and happening.{{/if}}}}{{else}}{{#if world_engine contains "FATE"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT, else 0; hp counts [hot] Bullets after this turn's loads, prunes and firings; last is this turn's tier, source and happening.}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{trim}}
Native reasoning: one pass through the plan lines, a terse bullet each, under 150 words{{#if world_engine contains "FATE" || world_engine contains "BONDS"}}, the Tally line aside{{/if}}; no drafts, rereads, rule audits or second passes, then write.
{{/if}}

